---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const analytics = /^G-[A-Z0-9]+$/.test((import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID || '').trim());
---
<Layout title="Privacy - Your files stay local | KittySuite" description="How KittySuite handles local files, font downloads, browser storage and website requests."><article class="shell section tool-details"><h1>Your files stay yours.</h1><p>Images, PDFs, text, HTML and signatures selected in our tools are processed on your device. Our tools do not send that content to a processing server, analytics endpoint or model API.</p><h2>What the website requests</h2><p>Your browser downloads the website and, when needed, processing libraries, a font index and selected font files from this site's host. These requests do not include your file contents or typed text. Like any website host, the hosting provider can receive request metadata such as your IP address, browser information and requested asset path.</p>{analytics ? <Fragment><h2>Analytics</h2><p>We use Google Analytics to count visits and simple tool events, such as a tool being opened, a file being selected, a task finishing or a download being clicked. These events contain the page address and a file count only. File names, file contents, typed text and form fields are never sent. Advertising features and Google signals are switched off. We do not show ads.</p></Fragment> : <p>We do not use ads, analytics or third-party trackers.</p>}<h2>Feedback form</h2><p>The feedback page is the only place where something you type leaves your device, and only when you press Send. The message, the optional name and email, and the tool you picked are sent to our form provider, Web3Forms, which forwards them to the KittySuite team by email. Files are never attached. Do not include passwords or personal documents.</p><h2>Storage and permissions</h2><p>Your theme and language preferences and a short list of tools you recently opened are stored in your browser so the homepage can show them again. They never leave your device. Fonts and site assets may be cached by the browser. Files are held in memory while a tool is open; reset or navigation releases working references. Downloads are saved where your browser chooses. Camera access is requested only when you choose to scan, and camera tracks stop when you finish or leave.</p><h2>Links and HTML</h2><p>Font source and licence links may open another site when you choose them. HTML tools remove scripts and external resources before rendering. They do not fetch URLs you paste. Browser extensions, the operating system and downloaded files are outside KittySuite's control.</p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>Local processing does not make every edit a security operation. Image blur is visual obfuscation. PDF crop hides edges without removing their underlying content. Redaction uses a separate raster rebuild workflow and discards the original PDF objects. Always review sensitive outputs before sharing.</p></article></Layout>
